# --- #1302 (part 3) --- the change marks of the non-block operators: a shift's '[ at the raw column
#     it started at, '] on the last line's last byte, '. at col 0 (op_shift); a join's '[ where the
#     first line ended, '] past the joined line, '. at col 0 of the line after it (do_join); gq's '] on
#     the cursor it leaves, '. where its last join or break was (op_format); a delete's '[ '] at its
#     start, '. at col 0 of the first deleted line or of the line after a joined start (op_delete); a
